                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game feels like dragging your balls through shards of glass. It’s the equivalent of cock and ball torture, and not the good kind. This game will slowly suck the life out of you, withering your soul until there’s nothing left but a hollow shell of the person you once were.\r\n\r\nYou’ll start feeling like you’re winning, like you’re finally getting the hang of things. You might even start having fun. You’ll sit back, crack your knuckles, and think, Holy shit, maybe I’m actually getting good at this. Then, out of nowhere, an entire team of players with names like Mild Cholester, pu$$yPwndR, PiddyCorn, blackGuy33444, and some guy named Jared will collectively turn your asshole into a war crime.\r\n\r\nNaturally, you’ll respond by going on a catastrophic losing streak, getting passed around like a hot piece of ass in a jail cell. Every match chips away at your sanity. Every teammate becomes a personal enemy. You’ll find yourself screaming at your monitor like a Victorian child who’s just watched his entire family die of tuberculosis. You’ll develop genuine, medically concerning hatred for people you’ve never met. You’ll start bargaining with whatever god might still be listening, promising to become a better person if only the next match doesn’t feature a teammate with the coordination of jacking off with your left hand and the emotional intelligence of a damp sock.\r\n\r\nAnd yet, somehow, you keep coming back.\r\n\r\nBecause this game is genuinely fun. Somewhere beneath the mountain of bullshit, buried under fourteen layers of psychological warfare and a matchmaking system seemingly designed by a lobotomised chimpanzee, there is a beautiful game desperately trying to escape. And every now and then, it does. You experience five glorious minutes of pure, unfiltered joy. You feel unstoppable. You feel alive. You feel like maybe, just maybe, everything is going to be okay.\r\n\r\nThen Jared queues up again.\r\n\r\nThis game will not simply take years off your life. It will make you spend those years wishing you had spent them doing literally anything else. You will emerge from every session a worse human being, carrying the emotional baggage of a divorced father of four and the blood pressure of a 90-year-old coal miner. Your family will ask you what's wrong. Your friends will notice the thousand-yard stare. You'll catch yourself clenching your jaw in the shower, thinking about a match from three days ago.\r\n\r\n10/10 experience. A masterpiece of human suffering. The only game where you can have the time of your life while actively wishing it to end. Play it to feel something again. Wouldn't recommend to anyone I love. (Fuck you Jared)",
